# Dev Client + same Wi‑Fi (no Cloudflare tunnel needed).
# 1) API:  uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
# 2) Put your laptop LAN IP below (Windows: ipconfig → IPv4 Address)
# 3) Phone + laptop on the same Wi‑Fi / hotspot
# 4) npm run start:dev  → open the Stride development build (not Expo Go)
#
# Native rebuild (homescreen icon, camera, reanimated, pose, etc.):
#    cd mobile
#    npm install
#    npx expo install --fix
#    npm run rebuild:dev:android
#      → EAS cloud APK (install from Expo dashboard / QR)
#    OR
#    npm run rebuild:local:android
#      → local USB / emulator build (needs Android SDK)
#
# After installing the new APK, uninstall the old Stride app first if the
# homescreen icon does not update (Android often caches launcher icons).
#
# Example: EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.5:8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://YOUR_LAN_IP:8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=http://YOUR_LAN_IP:3001
